					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/440-hertz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1249440); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1249440&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200920" alt="440 Hertz" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1249440)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/440-hertz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1249440); return false;" >440 Hertz</a></span> <span class="odate time_1547144648 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 Jan 2019 18:24</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4115041">
									

<p>I'm really thrilled that it was that engaging to you, my #1 goal with this item was to share the excitement that this simple thought experiment makes me feel (&quot;how much would two versions of me diverge if they started to have slightly different experiences right now? What would they think of each other?&quot;).</p>
<p>For what it's worth, my idea behind &quot;men and women tend to react differently, and someone with less marked sexual differentiation has more agency over the effects&quot; was as follows:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>In order to duplicate the mind, the prions use (among other things) vestigial structures in the male brain that would otherwise have been dedicated to &quot;female-ness&quot; (and vice-versa for females). I have no personal experience with gender dysphoria, but from what I can gather identity as a man or a woman is partially hardwired and has an incredibly strong effect on your conscious relationship with your body.<br />
It makes sense to me that one of the easiest way to make a distinct copy of someone's sense of self would be to take advantage of parts of the brain that get more active at the slightest input of testosterone/oestrogen, and that already deal with body image. Just like male nipples or female Gartner's duct, but in more subtle less well-understood brain structures!</p>
<p>So with all of that in mind, purely based on my questionable blurbs of biological justifications for the effects, the β consciousness of a nonbinary person would tend to match more closely with the gender opposite to the one assigned at birth!</p>
<p>While writing the SCP, at some point I started assigning a bit more importance to gender, but in the end I just kept it to make it very clear there is some logic behind the ability to control the effects (which is very precious to the Foundation), and thus justify the huge amount of research (if the effects were too unpredictable, it would not make sense to me that the Foundation would retain some hope of developing applications for the product).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

